{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1888 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "9b6796bf7fed1ddb2603972ff964b25712560884d9f79dd4d4f5010dc858b1b7" :edb/db-before-t 1887 :edb/db-after-t 1888 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535200 50 #inst "2026-10-08T19:25:00.119Z" 13194139535200 true] [17592186078129 1100 "A function $f(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| **$x$** | $0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $1$ | $1.1$ | $1.3$ | $1.7$ | $2.5$ |\n\nApproximate $f'(x)$ at the point $x=0.2$ using a central difference approximation." 13194139535200 true] [17592186078129 1100 "A function $f(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| **$x$** | $0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f(x)$ | $1$ | $1.1$ | $1.3$ | $1.7$ | $2.5$ |\n\nApproximate $f'(x)$ at the point $x=0.2$ using a central difference approximation." 13194139535200 false] [17592186078129 1145 "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\nf'(x) \\approx \\frac{f(x+h) - f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=0.2.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0.2) & ≈\\frac{f(0.2+0.1)-f(0.2-0.1)}{2(0.1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(0.3)-f(0.1)}{2(0.1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.7-1.1}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.6}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535200 true] [17592186078129 1145 "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\nf'(x) \\approx \\frac{f(x+h) - f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\nat the point $x=0.2$. We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.1$. This gives\n\n$$\nf^{′}(0.2) \\mid \\approx (f(0.2 + 0.1) - f(0.2 - 0.1))/(2(0.1)); = (f(0.3) - f(0.1))/(2(0.1)); = \\frac{1.7 - 1.1}{0.2}; = \\frac{0.6}{0.2}; = \\frac{6}{2}; = 3\n$$" 13194139535200 false] [17592186078130 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/assets/5355859a0307e46ae84d12bc5e0b183d72458972c8a417fb6d9296b4769ea078.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate $g'(x)$ at the point $x=4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=4.$" 13194139535200 true] [17592186078130 1100 "The graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above.\nApproximate $g'(x)$ at the point $x=4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=4$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/640/Source/Images/a750fcfca1b253b803c467e2619376fd.png)" 13194139535200 false] [17592186078130 1145 "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\ng'(x) \\approx \\dfrac{g(x+h) - g(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=4$ with step size $h=4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(4) & ≈\\frac{g(4+4)-g(4-4)}{2(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(8)-g(0)}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4-(-10)}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{8} \\\\  & =0.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535200 true] [17592186078130 1145 "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\ng'(x) \\approx \\dfrac{g(x+h) - g(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\nat the point $x=4$ with step size $h=4$. This gives\n\n$$\ng^{′}(4) \\mid \\approx (g(4 + 4) - g(4 - 4))/(2(4)); = (g(8) - g(0))/(8); = (-4 - (-10))/(8); = \\frac{6}{8}; = 0.75\n$$" 13194139535200 false] [17592186078133 1100 "A car engine is being heated from a temperature of about $-10^{\\circ}$. The temperature of the engine after $t$ minutes is given by $T(t)$. The graph of $T(t)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/640/Source/Images/2189fc374802d088f3c8ca4094372036.png)\n\nApproximate the rate at which the temperature of the engine increases when $t = 3$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1$." 13194139535200 false] [17592186078133 1100 "A car engine is being heated from a temperature of about $-10^{\\circ}.$ The temperature of the engine after $t$ minutes is given by $T(t).$  The graph of $T(t)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/assets/fe78a78911e2df9cdb488ec57b0e0a34bb56e18b57303d895dc8013b64a4afc3.png)\n\nApproximate the rate at which the temperature of the engine increases when $t = 3$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$" 13194139535200 true] [17592186078133 1145 "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\nT'(t) \\approx \\dfrac{T(t+h) - T(t-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\nat the time $t=3$ with step size $h=1$. This gives\n\n$$\nT^{′}(3) \\mid \\approx (T(3 + 1) - T(3 - 1))/(2(1)); = (T(4) - T(2))/(2); = \\frac{60 - 30}{2}; = \\frac{30}{2}; = 15\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of temperature increase is approximately $15^{\\circ}$ per minute." 13194139535200 false] [17592186078133 1145 "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\nT'(t) \\approx \\dfrac{T(t+h) - T(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\n \n\nat the time $t=3$ with step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{T(3+1)-T(3-1)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{T(4)-T(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{60-30}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{2} \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of temperature increase is approximately $15^{\\circ}$ per minute." 13194139535200 true] [17592186078525 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337105 13194139535200 true] [17592186078525 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337129 13194139535200 true] [17592186078525 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337133 13194139535200 true] [17592186078525 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337168 13194139535200 true] [17592186078526 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337112 13194139535200 true] [17592186078526 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337119 13194139535200 true] [17592186078526 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337136 13194139535200 true] [17592186078526 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337139 13194139535200 true] [17592186078526 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337143 13194139535200 true] [17592186078527 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337126 13194139535200 true] [17592186078527 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337147 13194139535200 true] [17592186078527 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337151 13194139535200 true] [17592186078527 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337154 13194139535200 true] [17592186078527 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337161 13194139535200 true] [17592186078783 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535200 true] [17592186078783 1100 "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nA function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| **$x$** | $-1.05$ | $-1$ | $-0.95$ | $-0.9$ | $-0.85$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $g(x)$ | $3.4$ | $2.5$ | $1.6$ | $2.1$ | $2.7$ |\n\nApproximate $g^{′}(x)$ at the point $x =-1$ using a central difference approximation." 13194139535200 false] [17592186078783 1100 "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| **$x$** | $-1.05$ | $-1$ | $-0.95$ | $-0.9$ | $-0.85$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $3.4$ | $2.5$ | $1.6$ | $2.1$ | $2.7$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=-1$ using a central difference approximation." 13194139535200 true] [17592186078783 1145 "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=-1.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.05.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(-1) & ≈\\frac{g(-1+0.05)-g(-1-0.05)}{2(0.05)} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(-0.95)-g(-1.05)}{2(0.05)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.6-3.4}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1.8}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-18}{1} \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535200 true] [17592186337105 1017 #edb/ref 17592186337106 13194139535200 true] [17592186337105 1089 "q-170649" 13194139535200 true] [17592186337105 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535200 true] [17592186337105 1100 "Given that $f(2.9)=5.91$ and $f(3.1)=7.11,$ find an approximation for ${f}^{′}(3).$" 13194139535200 true] [17592186337105 1113 #uuid "719885bd-89ec-5a69-9a1b-0bb3396c2432" 13194139535200 true] [17592186337105 1145 "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=3$ with the step size $h=0.1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h} \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{f(3+0.1)-f(3-0.1)}{2(0.1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(3.1)-f(2.9)}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7.11-5.91}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.2}{0.2} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535200 true] [17592186337106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337107 13194139535200 true] [17592186337106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337108 13194139535200 true] [17592186337106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337109 13194139535200 true] [17592186337106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337110 13194139535200 true] [17592186337106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337111 13194139535200 true] [17592186337106 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535200 true] [17592186337106 1041 "selection" 13194139535200 true] [17592186337106 1104 #edb/ref 17592186337109 13194139535200 true] [17592186337106 1110 #uuid "8fedd74f-c0bc-5a0a-acdd-b35d09ec210a" 13194139535200 true] [17592186337107 1034 "6.8" 13194139535200 true] [17592186337107 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535200 true] [17592186337107 1111 #uuid "f3036234-bc7e-5e96-b02a-80edd92bdbbd" 13194139535200 true] [17592186337108 1034 "2" 13194139535200 true] [17592186337108 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535200 true] [17592186337108 1111 #uuid "04718383-ec61-5d5c-94de-6f03f0603706" 13194139535200 true] [17592186337109 1034 "6" 13194139535200 true] [17592186337109 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535200 true] [17592186337109 1111 #uuid "991d0afd-0a94-5e0b-b85b-032097321c38" 13194139535200 true] [17592186337110 1034 "5.2" 13194139535200 true] [17592186337110 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535200 true] [17592186337110 1111 #uuid "447d8afa-f807-5765-9483-91b1e0741157" 13194139535200 true] [17592186337111 1034 "4" 13194139535200 true] [17592186337111 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535200 true] [17592186337111 1111 #uuid "ad7066b9-1fb6-5c8c-9847-d350fa37fff2" 13194139535200 true] [17592186337112 1017 #edb/ref 17592186337113 13194139535200 true] [17592186337112 1089 "q-170650" 13194139535200 true] [17592186337112 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535200 true] [17592186337